## Why This Is Asked

Tests candidate ability to design a mixed on-device/offload chat triage, evaluating lifecycle costs and business impact of privacy-preserving UX.

## Key Concepts

- On-device NLP model size and latency
- Cloud handoff economics
- Local storage and OTA updates
- Compliance and user trust
- Rollout and measurement plan

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for on-device classifier trigger
function triage(input) {
  const intent = onDeviceModel.predict(input);
  if (isComplex(intent)) {
    return cloudHandoff(input);
  }
  return generateResponse(intent);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure incremental savings from reduced cloud fetches?
- What telemetry would you collect to monitor quality without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about data integrity, offline-first design, and privacy/compliance trade-offs in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- offline-first data modeling
- tamper-evident logs (hash chaining)
- delta synchronization with encryption
- data retention and regulatory considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal hash chain for integrity check
function hashChain(entries) {
  let h = 0;
  for (const e of entries) h = (hashfunc(e) ^ h) >>> 0;
  return h;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model storage budget over 12 months?
- What are failure modes if delta sync fails or duplicates?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model a privacy-preserving on-device feature with federated updates, balancing memory, compute, energy, and compliance costs against business impact.

## Key Concepts

- On-device indexing and search
- Federated/update diffs with privacy guarantees
- Energy and latency trade-offs
- Compliance, data deletion, and auditability
- Break-even and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
function diffUpdate(localIndex, diff) {
  // apply partial updates safely
  // merge diff entries into local index
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(diff)) {
    localIndex[k] = v;
  }
  return localIndex;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would data deletion rights (GDPR/CCPA) be enforced on-device without leaking signals?
- How would you validate privacy guarantees and measure energy impact in field tests?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about client-side privacy, offline UX, and cost trade-offs without server trust. The candidate must specify concrete numbers, crypto choices, and go/no-go criteria, balancing performance, storage, and regulatory costs.

## Key Concepts

- Client-side encryption and key management
- Data growth and local cache sizing
- Delta synchronization vs full sync
- Privacy/compliance implications and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example using Web Crypto API AES-GCM
async function encrypt(plaintext, cryptoKey) {
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const encrypted = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(
    { name: 'AES-GCM', iv },
    cryptoKey,
    new TextEncoder().encode(plaintext)
  );
  return { encrypted, iv };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate a feature into a practical 12‑month CBA with edge constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference costs (latency, energy, memory)
- Privacy and data minimization
- Cloud review costs vs offline results
- Rollout strategy and drift/maintenance costs
- Break-even horizon selection

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateCBA(modelSizeMB, perInferenceJ, inferencesPerMonth, cloudCostPerEvent) {
  const energyKJ = perInferenceJ * inferencesPerMonth;
  const yearlyEnergyCost = (energyKJ / 1000) * 0.9;
  const cloudYear = cloudCostPerEvent * inferencesPerMonth * 12;
  const total = modelSizeMB + yearlyEnergyCost + cloudYear;
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify drift/maintenance costs and retraining cadence?
- How would latency targets influence model size vs accuracy trade-offs?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go?

